 href="#auth">Base URL & auth</a><a href="#routing">Gateway setup</a><a href="#api">API endpoints</a><a href="#webhooks">Webhooks</a><a href="#examples">Code examples</a><a href="#security">Security notes</a></nav><article class="docs-main"><div class="eyebrow">DEVELOPER DOCUMENTATION</div><h1>Build payments into your product.</h1><p>Integrate direct-to-merchant UPI checkout, then receive a status update from your configured payment-receipt workflow.</p><span class="pill pill-blue">API v1 · Starter implementation</span> <span class="pill pill-green"><i class="dot"></i> Deployment-dependent</span><div style="display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:22px 0"><code id="install">pip install -e ./sdk/python-sdk</code><button class="btn btn-outline" data-copy="#install">Copy</button><a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://pypi.org/project/tggateways/">PyPI page (if published) ↗</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://github.com/ShadowGamerIND37/tggateways">GitHub source ↗</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/openapi.json">OpenAPI JSON ↗</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/docs.txt">Plain-text reference ↗</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/llms.txt">llms.txt ↗</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/ai-prompt.txt">AI prompt ↗</a></div>
<div class="doc-callout">The code shown here is a self-hosted application and is not a payment aggregator. Merchant eligibility, account setup, settlement, provider fees, tax treatment and privacy obligations are determined by your providers and applicable law. Test in a controlled environment before production use.</div>
<h2 id="quickstart">Quick start</h2><ol><li>Deploy PHP 8.1+ with PDO MySQL, OpenSSL, cURL and Composer dependencies.</li><li>Import <code>database/schema.sql</code>; configure secrets in a private <code>.env</code>.</li><li>Provision an authenticated merchant and configure an active UPI account.</li><li>Send a server-side create-order request with your API key, then present the hosted checkout URL.</li><li>Set up and verify your receipt mailbox parser only after testing provider email formats. Configure a private cron.</li></ol><pre>composer install
mysql -u tggateways -p tggateways &lt; database/schema.sql
cp .env.example .env
# set APP_URL, DB_*, and a random 32-byte APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY</pre>
<h2 id="ai-context">Master AI agent context</h2><p>Copy this project-specific context into your coding assistant before asking it to extend the integration.</p><pre id="ai-prompt">You are helping integrate TG Gateways, a self-hosted PHP/MySQL application for direct-to-merchant UPI checkout. Do not claim it is a payment aggregator or that it holds funds. Use the configured API base URL and send the merchant API key only from a trusted server via X-Api-Key. Create an order with POST /api/create-order JSON {"amount":499.00,"customer_name":"Asha","redirect_url":"https://merchant.example/paid"}. Render checkout_url for the customer. Check status using GET /api/verify-order.php?order_id=... with server-side API-key auth. The public checkout-status endpoint is for display only and is not authoritative fulfillment proof. Verify the exact raw webhook request body using HMAC-SHA256 with the merchant API key and compare digests in constant time. Fulfill only once after signature verification and a successful payment event. The receipt IMAP parser is opt-in, depends on provider-specific receipt formats, and must be tested; never assume an email alone proves settlement unless validated. Keep all credentials server-side, store secrets encrypted, use HTTPS, respect UPI provider terms and limits, and consult qualified experts about applicable privacy, tax, consumer and payment rules. Database schema and routes live in this repository. Current API routes are documented in docs.php.</pre><button class="btn" data-copy="#ai-prompt">Copy Complete AI Prompt</button>
<h2 id="auth">Base URL & authentication</h2><p>Set your deployment's base URL. The example production domain shown in product copy is <code>https://tggateways.in</code>; use your actual HTTPS deployment URL.</p><pre>POST /api/create-order
X-Api-Key: tg_your_secret_key
Content-Type: application/json

Authorization: Bearer tg_your_secret_key</pre><p>API keys are merchant secrets. Do not expose them in browser JavaScript. The included API layer enforces a per-IP/per-operation request window; tune it to your server capacity. Polling every few seconds from every visitor can add load—prefer webhooks for fulfillment and use the public status endpoint only for checkout display.</p>
<h2 id="routing">Gateway setup & routing</h2><h3>UPI account & receipt mailbox</h3><ol><li>Configure an account through the merchant dashboard Integrations page.</li><li>Use a dedicated mailbox, enable IMAP, and create a scoped app password where supported.</li><li>The app password is encrypted with AES-256-GCM using the deployment's environment key. Set restrictive file permissions on <code>.env</code>.</li><li>Run <code>php cron/imap-parser.php</code> from a private scheduler. Monitor failures without logging message contents or credentials.</li><li>Validate parsing with your provider's current email format; adjust regex only from authorized test samples.</li></ol><div class="doc-callout">Never use multiple accounts to evade provider limits or account controls. Keep mailbox and financial-data access to the minimum required.</div>
<h2 id="api">Core API endpoints</h2><h3>1. Create order · POST /api/create-order</h3><pre>curl -X POST https://your-host.example/api/create-order \\
  -H 'X-Api-Key: tg_your_secret_key' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d '{"amount":499.00,"customer_name":"Asha","customer_email":"asha@example.com"}'</pre><pre>{"order_id":"tg_A1B2C3D4","qr_url":"https://your-deployment/api/qr-image.php?order_id=tg_A1B2C3D4","qr_path":"/api/qr-image.php?order_id=tg_A1B2C3D4","checkout_url":"https://your-deployment/pay.php?order_id=tg_A1B2C3D4","upi_intent":"upi://pay?...","payable_amount":"499.00","currency":"INR","status":"pending","expires_in_seconds":600}</pre><h3>2. Public checkout status · GET /api/checkout-status.php?order_id=…</h3><p>Returns display-safe order status and amount, with UTR hidden until success. Do not use this public route as your fulfillment authority.</p><h3>3. Server verification · GET /api/verify-order.php?order_id=…</h3><p>Requires API-key authentication; call from a trusted server.</p><h3>4. Hosted checkout · GET /pay.php?order_id=…</h3><p>Displays the QR, UPI-app intent shortcuts, countdown and status poller. Reusable links use <code>/pay.php?link=SLUG</code>.</p><h3>5. QR image · GET /api/qr-image.php?order_id=…</h3><p>Returns a PNG when Composer dependencies are installed. The image encodes a UPI payment intent for the configured active merchant account.</p><h3>6. Payment links · POST /api/manage-links.php</h3><pre>{"title":"Consultation","amount":499,"description":"Optional details"}</pre><p>GET on the same route lists the authenticated merchant's links.</p><h3>7. Transaction history · GET /api/get-transactions.php?status=success&amp;page=1&amp;limit=25</h3><p>Optional filters: <code>status</code> (pending, success, expired), <code>search</code> (order ID or UTR), <code>page</code> and <code>limit</code> (max 100).</p>
<h2 id="webhooks">Webhooks & HMAC-SHA256</h2><p>Events are sent as JSON. The signature is <code>sha256=hex(HMAC-SHA256(raw_body, merchant_api_key))</code> in <code>X-TGGateway-Signature</code>. Retry scheduling starts at approximately 5, 10 and 15 minutes, followed by a final bounded attempt. Make handlers idempotent by order ID.</p><pre>{"event":"payment.succeeded","order_id":"tg_A1B2C3D4","amount":499,"payable_amount":499,"status":"success","utr":"123456789012","transaction_id":"123456789012","paid_at":"2026-01-01 12:00:00"}</pre>
<h2 id="examples">Polyglot reference snippets</h2><h3>Python · SDK / requests</h3><pre>from tggateways import TGGateway
client = TGGateway("https://your-host.example", "tg_your_secret_key")
order = client.create_order(499.00, customer_name="Asha")
print(order["checkout_url"])
print(client.verify_order(order["order_id"])["status"])</pre><h3>Python · Webhook signature verification</h3><pre>import hmac, hashlib

def valid_signature(raw_body: bytes, header: str, api_key: str) -&gt; bool:
    supplied = header.removeprefix("sha256=")
    expected = hmac.new(api_key.encode(), raw_body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()
    return hmac.compare_digest(expected, supplied)</pre><h3>Node.js · Express listener</h3><pre>import express from 'express';
import crypto from 'node:crypto';
const app = express();
app.post('/webhooks/tg', express.raw({type:'application/json'}), (req,res) =&gt; {
  const supplied = (req.get('X-TGGateway-Signature') || '').replace(/^sha256=/, '');
  const expected = crypto.createHmac('sha256', process.env.TG_API_KEY).update(req.body).digest();
  let actual; try { actual = Buffer.from(supplied, 'hex'); } catch { return res.sendStatus(401); }
  if (actual.length !== expected.length || !crypto.timingSafeEqual(actual, expected)) return res.sendStatus(401);
  const event = JSON.parse(req.body.toString());
  // Verify event + idempotently fulfill successful order here.
  res.sendStatus(200);
});</pre><h3>PHP · cURL create order</h3><pre>$ch = curl_init('https://your-host.example/api/create-order');
curl_setopt_array($ch, [CURLOPT_POST =&gt; true,
  CURLOPT_HTTPHEADER =&gt; ['Content-Type: application/json', 'X-Api-Key: '.$apiKey],
  CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS =&gt; json_encode(['amount' =&gt; 499.00]), CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER =&gt; true]);
$response = curl_exec($ch);
$order = json_decode($response, true);</pre><h3>PHP · Verify webhook</h3><pre>$raw = file_get_contents('php://input');
$header = $_SERVER['HTTP_X_TGGATEWAY_SIGNATURE'] ?? '';
$expected = 'sha256='.hash_hmac('sha256', $raw, $apiKey);
if (!hash_equals($expected, $header)) { http_response_code(401); exit; }
$event = json_decode($raw, true);</pre>
<h2 id="security">Security & privacy notes</h2><ul><li>Webhook URL configuration must be locked down against SSRF before public production deployment.</li><li>UTR uniqueness and row locks help prevent duplicate assignment; reconcile with provider records and handle unmatched receipts operationally.</li><li>Do not store customer payment credentials. Limit access to mailbox receipts and promptly delete data not needed for operations.</li><li>HTTPS, strict secrets handling, backups, audit logging without secrets, dependency updates, and incident response are deployment responsibilities.</li><li>No claim of legal compliance or GST exemption is made by this software. Obtain professional advice for your facts and jurisdiction.</li></ul><p><a href="/">← Back to TG Gateways</a></p></article></main><script src="/assets/js/main.js"></script></body></html>
